  "rationale": "The representative error assigns most probability to <END> after a comma, because its broad existing punctuation rule treats commas like sentence-final punctuation. Across the batch, commas frequently introduce a person, and the four observed person tokens should remain alternatives rather than being inferred from a specific name. Reduce that broad <END> rule while retaining the existing explicit closing rule, and add a reusable comma-suffix rule to each observed person token. The batch also repeatedly uses And so, And that, and that was, while those output roots currently have little matching mass; add lexical, context-specific rules for these patterns. These generalizations may overpredict a person after commas in other constructions or favor these continuations in contexts where alternatives are valid; the replay gate must assess that risk. The free-generation sample is not treated as training evidence.",
